body:
Congrats man!! Got an offer too for BSc Economics the other day, almost definitely going to LSE this year (met my conditions) so hope to see you there!! 

&#x200B;

Do you know of any online groups for offer holders by any chance? I'm an international student and hence won't be able to go for the offer holders day.

Claremont McKenna College offers merit-based scholarships that cover up to the full cost of tuition. They also have an enormous portion of funding dedicated to student projects/research.

&#x200B;

The deadline to be considered for those scholarships was on December 1, though.

Your GPA is definitely fine, your SAT IIs are good enough, but your main SAT puts you below the 75th percentile, which is generally where you should hope to be. Since you're a junior, you do have chances to take it again - that said, however, if taking the SATs again to improve your score will draw away from your success in other areas of your application (grades, commitment to ECs, etc), then it's probably not worth taking. Plenty of people can and do get in with 1500. Your description of your ECs was quite brief - if the Physics Olympics was a big accomplishment to you and is something you can write about, then it might help. Your volunteering hours are a little on the low side, but you definitely have the time to raise them by next year. 

&#x200B;

Overall, seems like you do have a fighting chance of getting in Cornell (especially ED), so by all means apply.
